# Stamped into every project `bgate init` creates.
#
# THIS FILE EXISTS BECAUSE THE DOCUMENTED SETUP LEAKED A KEY. The README tells
# you to put OPENAI_API_KEY / KREA_API_KEY in a .env at your GAME PROJECT's
# root, and it also tells you that `.bgate/game.db` travels with the repo --
# which means the natural next step is `git init` in this directory. Without
# this file, following both instructions commits the key.
#
# Builders Gate's own repo learned that lesson once already; its .gitignore
# still carries the note. The fix there only covered the tool's repo, not the
# project the tool GENERATES, which is where the README actually tells you to
# put the key.

# API keys.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Per-project store. Contains the dashboard's auth token, so it is ignored by
# default. If you deliberately want the game DB in version control, remove this
# line AND rotate the token -- do not do one without the other.
.bgate/

# Adapter scratch: renders, playtest captures, logs. Regenerated, never sourced.
.bgate_out/

# Godot's import cache and per-machine export config.
.godot/
export_presets.cfg

# NOT ignored, deliberately: *.import files carry import settings and the
# resource UID. Without them a clone re-imports and can renumber UIDs, which
# breaks every scene reference that resolves by uid://.

# Blender
*.blend1
*.blend2
